  "term": "lateral preoptic area",
  "definition": "The lateral preoptic area is an anatomical subregion examined alongside parts of the lateral hypothalamus in research on eating and reward-related behavior. In the cited study, optogenetic stimulation of this area produced relatively little food intake or self-stimulation compared with some nearby lateral hypothalamic subregions.",
